2025-05-01 02:26:15 - Thread-853 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "project_short_name": identify TCGA‑BRCA rows  
• "sample_type_name": pick only Solid Tissue Normal samples  
• "gene_type": keep only protein_coding genes  
• "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ": expression value whose variance we want  
• "case_barcode": connect samples that belong to the same case  
• "sample_barcode": differentiate samples inside a case  
• "gene_name" / "Ensembl_gene_id": gene identifiers needed for “top five” list  

Typical filter conditions  
• "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
• "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'  (use ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' when unsure)  
• "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'  
• Case restriction: keep only cases that contain at least one Solid Tissue Normal sample, e.g.  
  WHERE "case_barcode" IN (SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"  
                            FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28  
                            WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
                              AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal')

Ten exploratory SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows)  
```sql
-- 1. Description: List every distinct sample type appearing in TCGA‑BRCA to verify the exact label for “Solid Tissue Normal”.
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show 20 TCGA‑BRCA cases that have at least one Solid Tissue Normal sample.
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Confirm that “protein_coding” exists in gene_type for BRCA rows.
SELECT DISTINCT "gene_type"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Peek at 20 expression rows for Solid Tissue Normal samples and protein‑coding genes.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Check the numeric range of HTSeq__FPKM_UQ for such rows.
SELECT MIN("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS min_val,
       MAX("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS max_val,
       AVG("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS avg_val
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Show 20 genes with count of Solid Tissue Normal samples (ensuring enough observations for variance).
SELECT "gene_name",
       COUNT(*) AS sample_cnt
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name"
ORDER BY sample_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Compute sample variance of HTSeq__FPKM_UQ per gene (quick look at 20 genes).
SELECT "gene_name",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS var_fpkm_uq
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name"
ORDER BY var_fpkm_uq DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Restrict to cases that definitely have ≥1 Solid Tissue Normal sample (subquery), preview 20 rows.
SELECT r."case_barcode",
       r."sample_barcode",
       r."gene_name",
       r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28 r
WHERE r."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND r."gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
  AND r."case_barcode" IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
        FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
          AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
      )
  AND r."sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as query 7 but using “Ensembl_gene_id” (gene names can duplicate); returning top 20 by variance.
SELECT "Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS var_fpkm_uq
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "Ensembl_gene_id"
ORDER BY var_fpkm_uq DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query to obtain the top 5 protein‑coding genes with the highest expression variance in Solid Tissue Normal samples from TCGA‑BRCA (limited to 20 rows as requested, although only 5 returned).
SELECT "gene_name",
       "Ensembl_gene_id",
       VAR_SAMP("HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS var_fpkm_uq
FROM TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R28
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" = 'Solid Tissue Normal'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "gene_name", "Ensembl_gene_id"
ORDER BY var_fpkm_uq DESC
LIMIT 20;   -- top 5 genes will appear at the top of this 20‑row window
```
